  <h2 id="who">Who handles refunds</h2>
  <p>Our order process is conducted by our online reseller Paddle.com. Paddle.com is the Merchant of Record for all our orders, and refunds are issued by Paddle to your original payment method, usually within 5–10 business days.</p>

  <h2 id="14-days">14-day refund</h2>
  <p>Ask within 14 days of a payment. We refund what you paid, minus the translation time you used from that payment at $3 per hour and Paddle’s payment processing cost (5% of the amount paid plus $0.50). If nothing is left, there is no refund. This applies to every payment: your first payment, monthly renewals, extra hours and day passes. For example, if you paid $19 for Basic and used 2 hours, we refund $19 − $6 − $1.45 = $11.55. You do not need to give a reason.</p>

  <h2 id="after-refund">What a refund does to your plan</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A refund ends what that payment gave you. If it is the payment for your current billing period (your first payment or a renewal), that subscription ends immediately. A refunded day pass ends, and the hours from a refunded extra-hours purchase are removed from your balance (down to zero, not below). Refunding an earlier period’s payment doesn’t end a current period you paid for separately.</li>
    <li>If any subscription payment, including an upgrade’s price difference, is charged back, the subscription ends immediately.</li>
    <li>A refund of an upgrade’s price difference keeps your plan and removes the included hours that upgrade added.</li>
    <li>An outage refund (below) is a partial refund that keeps your plan. If it covers extra hours, a day pass or an upgrade’s price difference, we remove the refunded share of those hours.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="hours">When hours become available</h2>
  <p>Included hours for a billing period become available once that period’s payment completes. If a renewal payment fails, that period’s hours are added once it is paid.</p>

  <h2 id="plan-changes">Changing plans</h2>
  <p>An upgrade takes effect immediately: the price difference for the rest of the current billing period is charged pro rata, and the difference in included hours is added for the rest of that period on the same basis. A downgrade also takes effect immediately, with no charge or refund for the current period: you keep the current period’s hours, and your next bill is at the lower price. Downgrading does not limit the 14-day refund above.</p>

  <h2 id="cancel">Cancelling</h2>
  <p>You can cancel any time in Account › Plan &amp; billing. Your plan stays active until the end of the period you paid for and does not renew. Extra hours you bought never expire.</p>
  <p>Deleting your account cancels your subscription automatically (Paddle may take a little while to confirm the cancellation) and removes any unused extra hours. You can still ask for a refund through <a href="https://paddle.net">paddle.net</a> within 14 days of a payment.</p>

  <h2 id="outages">Outages</h2>
  <p>If a service outage on our side stops you using Tolkmeet for 24 hours or more, we refund the affected part of that billing period’s plan on request, even after 14 days.</p>

  <h2 id="legal-rights">Your legal rights</h2>
  <p>Nothing here limits rights you have under consumer protection law where you live, such as withdrawal rights in the European Union or Korea. Translation time starts to be provided as soon as your payment completes, so where the law allows, a withdrawal right ends once you start using it.</p>

  <h2 id="how-to-ask">How to ask</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Through Paddle: go to <a href="https://paddle.net">paddle.net</a>, find your order with the email address you paid with, and request a refund.</li>
    <li>Or email billing@tolkmeet.com from, or including, the email address on your account.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Your receipts are under Account › Plan &amp; billing › Payment method &amp; receipts.</p>
</Legal>
